# Elm compilation output + sidecar fingerprints. The compiled kernel
# JS is generated by `scripts/build-elm.sh` against this tree's
# tracked Elm sources. The `.sha256` sidecars are emitted alongside
# so the build orchestrator can verify the produced JS byte-for-byte
# before staging it into the dogfood artifact.
#
# Mirrors `completion-continuation-control/.gitignore` exactly per
# ACT-CLINEMM-ELMIZE-P1-TOOLCHAIN-RESOLVER01. The Elm compiler is
# a toolchain input, not source: the canonical dogfood builder
# resolves the pinned compiler on the build host and passes it via
# `${ELM_BIN}` into the kernel's `build-elm.sh`. Keeping the
# 60 MB binary out of every tracked kernel also makes the
# exact-HEAD worktree reproducible without injecting files into the
# temporary detached worktree.
#
# `scripts/elm_toolchain.sh` will still consult `${HERE}/vendor/elm`
# as a fallback if a developer drops one in for local builds; the
# `.gitignore` keeps it excluded so it can never leak into a commit.
vendor/*.js
vendor/*.js.sha256
vendor/elm
vendor/elm.sha256
vendor/elm.gz
vendor/elm.version
elm-stuff/
.elm-home/
